select 'Korea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology (KAIST)','South Korea','Public','University','Daejeon','https://www.kaist.ac.kr/en/',false,false,'{"ug": "KAIST teaches in English: its official language of instruction for international students is English, and few courses are in Korean (international students can take English-taught substitutes). Students enter with an undeclared major and choose any department at the end of the first year, with no quota per department. There is no transfer route; everyone starts as a freshman. Students from English-speaking countries, or whose high school taught in English, can be exempt from the English test. Only some of KAIST''s departments are listed here; see the admissions page for all of them.", "sources": ["https://admission.kaist.ac.kr/intl-undergraduate/before/sub01"]}'::jsonb,'https://admission.kaist.ac.kr/intl-undergraduate/before/sub01',date '2026-11-27'
